---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import { SEO, SITE } from '../config/site';
const updated = '23 October 2026';
---
<BaseLayout title={SEO.privacy.title} description={SEO.privacy.description}>
  <PageHead title="Privacy policy" lead={`How ${SITE.name} handles your personal information. Last updated ${updated}.`} crumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy policy' }]} />
  <section class="band-sm">
    <div class="wrap"><div class="prose-fk">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Who we are</h2>
      <p>{SITE.name} (“FoxKey”, “we”, “us”) is a mobile auto locksmith and vehicle diagnostics business based in {SITE.baseTown}, {SITE.baseRegion}, United Kingdom. We are the data controller for the personal information described in this policy. You can contact us by phone or WhatsApp on {SITE.phoneDisplay}.</p>

      <h2>What information we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Enquiry forms</strong>: name, phone number, company name (fleet enquiries), vehicle details (type, make, model, year, registration where given), vehicle location or postcode and the content of your message.</li>
        <li><strong>Phone and WhatsApp</strong>: your number and the content of calls or messages you send us.</li>
        <li><strong>Proof of ownership</strong>: before key, immobiliser or module work we inspect your V5C logbook and photo ID (or operator authorisation). We check these in person; we may record that the check was carried out and the registration worked on, but we do not keep copies of your ID unless you agree.</li>
        <li><strong>Payment information</strong>: card payments are processed by our card-terminal provider; we do not store card numbers.</li>
        <li><strong>Technical data</strong>: our hosting provider may log basic request data (IP address, browser type, pages requested) for security and performance.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why we use it and our lawful basis</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To respond to your enquiry, quote and carry out the work you ask for (<em>performance of a contract / steps before a contract</em>).</li>
        <li>To verify you are entitled to have keys or modules programmed to a vehicle, and to keep a record of that verification (<em>legal obligation and legitimate interests</em>, preventing vehicle theft and fraud).</li>
        <li>To issue invoices and keep accounting records (<em>legal obligation</em>).</li>
        <li>To keep the website secure (<em>legitimate interests</em>).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not use your information for marketing unless you ask us to, and we do not sell it.</p>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Formspree</strong>: processes website form submissions and forwards them to us. See <a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Formspree’s privacy policy</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Meta Platforms (WhatsApp)</strong>: if you contact us via WhatsApp, your messages are handled under WhatsApp’s terms.</li>
        <li><strong>Google</strong>: the Contact page embeds a Google Map, which may set cookies and collect usage data when loaded. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google’s privacy policy</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Our website host</strong> (e.g. Cloudflare or Netlify), serves the site and may log technical data.</li>
        <li>Our accountant and payment provider, where needed to process payments and keep records.</li>
        <li>The police or other authorities where required by law, for example in connection with suspected vehicle theft.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>Enquiry details are kept for up to 12 months after our last contact unless they become part of a job record. Job and invoicing records are kept for 6 years as required for tax purposes. Ownership-verification records are kept with the job record.</p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>This site uses a single essential item of local storage to remember that you have dismissed the cookie notice. We do not use analytics or advertising cookies. The Google Maps embed on the Contact page may set third-party cookies when it loads. You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings.</p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under UK GDPR you have the right to access the personal information we hold about you, to have it corrected or erased, to restrict or object to its processing, and to data portability. To exercise any of these rights, contact us on {SITE.phoneDisplay}. You also have the right to complain to the Information Commissioner’s Office (ICO) at <a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener" target="_blank">ico.org.uk</a>.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top shows when it was last changed.</p>
    </div></div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
